																		IT&#039;S HAPPENING
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=388108&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973900" alt="Djoric" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=388108)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;" >Djoric</a></span> <span class="odate time_1418599338 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Dec 2014 23:22</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2179953">
									

<p>Part 1 of 3(?)</p>
<p>Also, jenssosaurus is kinda the best at <a href="http://i.imgur.com/IexXE6s.jpg">fanart</a>.</p>
<p>E: For those of you unfamiliar with Russian folk songs, Nanami opens her sequence with the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BiSx5LCnugw">Volga Boatmen Song</a>. Her choice of Air on the G string is in reference to that one sequence from <em>End of Evangelion</em> (you know the one). Her hostmasks involve, in order:</p>
<p>1) Aposematic coloration, which is the possession of bright warning colors<br />
2) Another Asuka reference, plus a little Soviet / Warhammer 40k morale boosting<br />
3) The main antagonist of <em>Mossflower</em><br />
4&amp;5) Two that don't actually have any references<br />
6) A vodka-swilling demon who takes the form of a little girl in a china doll dress, from the BPRD comics</p>
<p>Benedict Cumberpidgeon is an oblique reference to <em>Hatoful Boyfriend</em>, and Momoko's hobby of gunsmithery is an entirely unintentional but very welcome retroactive reference to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bXE4wO-Qt48">Gunsmith Cats</a>.</p>

							</div>

								
