					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crawldragon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1935528); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1935528&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973900" alt="Crawldragon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1935528)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/crawldragon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1935528); return false;" >Crawldragon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1418607551 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Dec 2014 01:39</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2180035">
									

<p>I imagine a bunch of people are going to downvote this because &quot;it's not in the spirit of the Foundation,&quot; because &quot;it's not scary,&quot; or &quot;this site isn't for happy bouncy stories, it's for grimdark and horror.&quot; <span style="color: red">Fuck those people.</span></p>
<p>It's rare that I get to see a story like this anywhere, let alone on the SCP site, and you know what? Fuck it. The Foundationverse deserves to have a reasonably light-spirited story happen in it once in a god damn blue moon, and I approve of this shift in tone. I haven't seen a Tale on this site that delighted me so much since the days of decommissionings, and I'm gonna upvote the shit out of this Tale because it made me <em>care</em>.</p>
<p>More than that, it made me care about characters that aren't even human, so bonus points.</p>

							</div>

								
					
