				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="1361261"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1418762340 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Dec 2014 20:39</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2182031">
									

<p>This is far, far too silly for me to support. The bits with Alexandra especially.</p>
<p>However, I have no issues with the writing itself, and I do note that unlike the original article, the dialogue between the various characters is now distinguishable; each of the individual members of the team has, if not a developed personality, at least their own voice. Lack of characterization and hideous dialogue are the things that plague a lot of tales, and this one has avoided those issues.</p>
<p>Also, this seems much more focused upon story and narrative than the initial entry. I don't think it's ever going to be entirely free of out-of-universe baggage, but I much prefer this take on the idea, where things are allowed to happen as dictated by what the <em>narrative</em> demands.</p>
<p>No way in this lifetime I'm upvoting cyber-furries, but the solid writing and improvement upon the concept demand a neutral vote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
